id: E1002-draft-2301_80739235
trigger_tool: conan|autotools|cmake|w64devkit|ohos-cross
phase: conan_build|consumer_build|target_validation
error_signature: "syntax error: unexpected (|no acceptable ld found in $PATH|cannot find input file: `F'|inappropriate file type or format|dummy.c: Permission denied|TMPDIR"
severity: 2
category: ohos|windows-hosted|path-quoting|toolchain|conan
match_keywords: Windows-hosted OHOS build, w64devkit POSIX wrapper, compiler tool identity, drive-letter config.status, CMake shell-wrapper execution
title: Windows-hosted OHOS builds need separate Autoconf and CMake tool identities
root_cause: A Conan recipe crossed incompatible execution boundaries. w64devkit invokes compiler paths through a POSIX shell, so Bash arrays and space-bearing tool paths fail; old Autoconf also splits generated F:/ source paths at the drive colon. Windows CMake can compile through a shell wrapper from make but cannot directly execute that .sh wrapper for its link step. OHOS workers may additionally expose a shared TMPDIR that denies package writes; a generated toolchain env file can be overridden by the worker process environment, so config.guess still fails before compilation unless the recipe process and shell wrapper both bind temporary probes to the task build directory.
affected_scope: Conan recipes using Autotools or CMake with a Windows build context and an OHOS cross compiler whose SDK or task paths contain spaces.
verification_cmd: "sh -n <posix-wrapper>; conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<windows-profile>; conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<linux-profile>; verify generated TMPDIR is task-local and writable"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: task-private-tool-identity-contract
rec_description: Use POSIX-compatible task-local wrappers for the Autoconf phase and bind LD, AR, RANLIB, NM, and STRIP; keep shell utilities and make under a no-space task path; invoke legacy Autoconf from the build directory with a relative configure path so config.status never parses a drive colon as a template separator; on OHOS workers bind TMPDIR to the writable task build folder in the generated environment, the recipe process environment, and any task shell wrapper, pass an explicit build triplet when legacy config.guess cannot write its mktemp dummy probe, use umask 022 for worker ACLs that reject private config.status files, provide a task-local mktemp shim when the worker rejects private subdirectories, and explicitly bind PATH-resolved bash to SHELL/CONFIG_SHELL so Autoconf and libtool do not mix incompatible shell builtins. For a Windows-hosted CMake consumer, resolve the wrapper's native clang.exe identity and carry its target, quoted sysroot, lld, and platform flags into one custom CMakeToolchain instance.
rec_command: "bind CC/CXX/LD/AR/RANLIB/NM/STRIP; use relative configure; resolve native clang.exe for Windows CMake; carry --target, quoted --sysroot, -fuse-ld=lld and platform flags; read back RC and consumer build output"
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: native-wsl-build
fallback_description: WSL/Linux can validate the current OHOS recipe and consumer without the Windows CMake direct-execution boundary, but it does not prove a Windows-hosted CMake consumer can execute a .sh compiler wrapper.
fallback_command: "conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=default"
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: "run a Bash-array wrapper under w64devkit sh|leave LD as a space-bearing host path"
forbid_1_reason: w64devkit may ignore the Bash shebang and Autoconf invokes the wrapper with a POSIX shell; the host path is then split or treated as a command prefix.
forbid_1_consequence: Configure reports C compiler cannot create executables or no acceptable ld found in PATH.
forbid_2_pattern: "invoke legacy Autoconf with an absolute F:/ source path"
forbid_2_reason: Berkeley DB's generated config.status uses colon-separated input templates, so a Windows drive colon becomes a bogus template named F.
forbid_2_consequence: config.status fails with cannot find input file F and no Makefile is generated.
forbid_3_pattern: "claim Windows CMake consumer PASS from a package-only or WSL result"
forbid_3_reason: Windows CMake may execute a .sh wrapper for compile through make but cannot CreateProcess the same wrapper for the direct link command; WSL exercises a different host boundary.
forbid_3_consequence: The library package can be valid while the Windows test_package consumer fails with inappropriate file type or format.
forbid_4_pattern: "leave TMPDIR bound to a non-writable shared worker cache|rely on config.guess mktemp when worker ACL denies dummy.c|leave umask 077 for config.status private files on ACL-restricted workers|use system mktemp when worker rejects private subdirectories|allow Autoconf to select a different shell from libtool"
forbid_4_reason: Legacy config.guess creates dummy compiler probes through TMPDIR before it can report the build system; a shared cache may be readable but deny package writes.
forbid_4_consequence: OHOS CI fails during configure with dummy.c or subs1.awk permission denied even though the source and compiler are valid, or config.status emits print-not-found and libtool syntax errors; an explicit build triplet, task wrapper umask 022, task-local mktemp shim, and one consistent bash shell are required when worker boundaries differ.
principles: P003, P007, P018
